		<Owner Company="Sigmatek"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.23" Date="2025-12-09" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Internal assignments are following the strict exact ENUM type exact type checking rules.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: Added feature of axis couple check to allow a reaction of the profile movement to a decoupled axes. See methods ReadAxisCoupleCheck() and SetAxisCoupleCheck().&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: Improved method comments of class."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.22" Date="2025-05-09" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: Content of internal spline structure used for MoveCurve() commands of _LMCRobotBase are now correctly cleared, when the path length is zero.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: Added new method GetHWAxisAllStatus() to read the combined AxisStatus information of all connected HW axes objects."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.21" Date="2025-03-12" Author="HatTim&#13;&#10;StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Added support for torque limited drive to class. Torque limited drive is a feature for _LMCAxis to allow following a torque limited axes to avoid acceleration jumps, when torque limitation is changed.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: Added feature for fast transition to allow accelerating or decelerting inside of transition. Mode can be activated via flag FastTransition in CmdConfig input parameter of move command.&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: Internal performance improvements. See revision description of _LMCProfileBase 3.49 for further details."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.20" Date="2023-07-26" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Private methods AxPowerOn() and AxPowerOff() are defined as virtual to allow user specific implementation of the methods.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: Some pointer accesses were not done in a threadsafe manner."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.19" Date="2023-06-14" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: When the robot is powered on in _ACTIVE mode the Override of the connected axis was written to 1000, when the write method of Override server was called. The override value written to the connected axis is now the written value on the override server. "/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.18" Date="2022-09-13" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Following private methods are now virtual private methods. DirKinematic(), InvKinematic(), UpdatePosServer(), RobPassiveToActive(), RobPassiveToDirect(), RobPassiveToError(), RobActiveToPassive(), RobActiveToDirect(), RobActiveToError(), RobDirectToPassive(), RobDirectToActive(), RobDirectToError(), RobErrorToPassive(), RobErrorToDirect() and RobErrorToActive().&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: Object channel calls of not required clients like LMCCalcModel or LMCBaseCoord are not used."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.17" Date="2022-05-19" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: A clothoid transition used on a belt coupling command leads to wrong movement on belt level inside of the axis software limits. A belt coupling move command with a clothoid transition or when the previous command has a programmed clothoid transition is denied.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: When the sw limit check was deactivated a position overflow or underflow can occur, when the profile position was exceeding the maximum or minimum value of DINT data type at relative movements.&#13;&#10;3. Bugfix: If a move command with MoveImmediately option is used to decouple from a belt by changing the coordinate system an access exception occurs."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.16" Date="2022-04-22" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: By writing on one of the following servers VMax, AMax, JMax the maximum tangential error and the profile offset is resetted to their respective default value."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.15" Date="2021-11-26" Author="StePhi&#13;&#10;SakEmi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: MoveCurveSpline movements must have an exact stop at the beginning and at the end. Move commands with any other type of transition are not processed correctly. The transition type in front and after a MoveCurveSpline movement are now automatically changed to be an exact stop.&#13;&#10;2. BugFix: Resolution considered by internal belt method calls&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: No movements or profile lock allowed during spline movement calculation&#13;&#10;4. Improvement: New input CoordSystem added in the method GetStartPositions. It determines the coordinate system in which the start positions are delivered. If no coordinate system is specified (=0), the start position is given in world coordinates.&#13;&#10;5. BugFix: Interrupt movements with bit MoveImmediately are properly handled if the movement is set while the robot is waiting for the conveyor belt at the SW limit (_LMCBELT_WAIT4BELT_WAITCOUPLE)&#13;&#10;6. Improvement: Path length of a spline movement is now calculated by multiplication."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.14" Date="2021-11-25" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Bugfix: A velocity jump in one single tick can happen, when the robot gets decoupled from a belt with a MoveLinearBelt command."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.13" Date="2021-11-23" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: In case of belt-coupling a temporary decouple was possible leading to undesired wobbles in the velocity in belt direction.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: In case of belt-coupling, when the robot movement decouples from the belt undesired wobbles in the velocity in belt direction can happen."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.12" Date="2021-08-18" Author="StePhi&#13;&#10;SakEmi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Added a tangential axis feature to define an axis which is dragged by the movement of two other axis with an optional offset to the tangential direction and a maximum angle of the transition angle jump.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: Define constant CIRCLE3D_NO_HELIX_MAX_DEVIATION is not defined twice when _LMCCNCKinematic class is used too."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.11" Date="2021-06-23" Author="StePhi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Bugfix: A monotonic desired trajectory with no linear start and/or end movement is now performed correclty without an additional vertical movement higher than the desired position."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.10" Date="2021-03-23" Author="SakEmi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="BugFix: Calculation inaccuracy in UpdateBeltAxisSWLimits_RotDisc corrected. Coupling to a rotational belt enabled."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.9" Date="2020-10-15" Author="StePhi&#13;&#10;HasHan&#13;&#10;SakEmi" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Added method to return pointer to KinAxisAllStatus information.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: an internal override can now be used with a connected _LMCCalcModelBase&#13;&#10;3. Bugfix: The method ValueToIntLREAL() was integrated to prevent a loss of decimal places.&#13;&#10;4. Improvement: the methode UpdateAxStatus() is now virtual = true&#13;&#10;5. Bugfix: MoveCurve() movements are now performed smoothly in case of an obstacle with an higher end height of the linear movement as the end height of the first curved movement.&#13;&#10;6. Improvement: Reverse drive by changing the sign of the server Override value enabled."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.8" Date="2020-04-02" Author="SakEmi&#13;&#10;VelGer" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Immediate direction change to a new, interrupt target possible&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: A StopMove(3, &lt;&gt; 0), which interrupts a BeltCoupling-command, will not end up with EndProfile"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.7" Date="2020-02-02" Author="VelGer&#13;&#10;HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: MoveCurveSpline(), MoveCurveSplineBelt() and MoveCurveSplineCoord() functionality added.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: If the robot is already at the target pos when a MoveXXXBelt() command was called, the move was stopped with an error, this is now handled as expected.&#13;&#10;3. BugFix: If StopMove() was called whilst coupled to a stationary Conveyor Belt, the decoupling time was calculated incorrectly, this is now corrected."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.6" Date="2019-06-24" Author="VelGer" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Added Comments regarding ThreadSafety to the following Methods:&#13;&#10;-MoveLinearBelt&#13;&#10;-MoveCurveBelt&#13;&#10;-LockProfile&#13;&#10;-UnlockProfile&#13;&#10;-MoveLinear&#13;&#10;-MoveCircle&#13;&#10;-MoveRelative&#13;&#10;-MoveCurve&#13;&#10;-MoveEndless&#13;&#10;-MoveLinearCoord&#13;&#10;-MoveCurveCoord&#13;&#10;-MoveEndlessCoord&#13;&#10;-MoveRelativeTCP&#13;&#10;-MoveCircleCoord&#13;&#10;-MoveRelativeCoord"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.5" Date="2019-05-24" Author="HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Bugfix: MoveCurveBelt() directly after a LockProfile() now operates as expected."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.4" Date="2019-05-23" Author="VelGer" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Improvement: Fixed new compiler version warnings in base and included class (W0172 &amp; W0173)."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.3" Date="2019-04-11" Author="SatChr&#13;&#10;HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: New functionality for coupling to a rotatory disc with MoveLinearBelt and MoveCurveBelt.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: Various bugs in belt coupling with belt couple factor &lt;&gt; 1 or resolution factor &lt;&gt; 1 corrected.&#13;&#10;3. Bugfix: Avoid jump of the setposition in combination with belt coupling and error _LMCPROF_ProfileInPos_Timeout&#13;&#10;4. Bugfix: Avoid DivisionError with too big MoveCurve input parameters Obstacle.VelStart_relativ_ppT and VelEnd_relativ_ppT.&#13;&#10;5. Improvement: Prevent to call User_CheckValidPositions() with a position input parameter _VOID_POS.&#13;&#10;6. Improvement: the clients LMCPre/PostRtWorkTrigger are now connected to the outside of the class"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.2" Date="2018-12-05" Author="HasHan&#13;&#10;SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: StopMove() at active belt-coupling with no active movement works now correct&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: The MoveCurve parameters Obstacle.VelStart_relativ_ppT and Obstacle.VelEnd_relativ_ppT have been ignored since _LMCRobotBase v2.0&#13;&#10;3. Bugfix: The MoveCurve arc is not longer related to the world coordinate system, if start coordinate system equals the new coordinate system. Bug since _LMCRobotBase v2.0&#13;&#10;4. Bugfix: Smoother MoveCurve movement at the transition from linear movement to the arc. Adaptions for new version 1.1 of embedded class _LMCTableBuffer."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.1" Date="2018-10-01" Author="SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. BugFix: Suppress compiler warnings with old Lasal Class2 version."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="2.0" Date="2017-11-23" Author="HasHan&#13;&#10;PalHar&#13;&#10;SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Revised command MoveCurve() with better dynamical behaviour.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: various improvement with belt coupling like software limit handling, monitoring dynamical limits,...&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: new move commands MoveEndless and MoveEndlessCoord added.&#13;&#10;4. Improvement: changed interface User_CheckValidPositions().&#13;&#10;5. Improvement: new method ConnectAxis()&#13;&#10;6. Bugfix: RobotOn() does not return ACCESS_DENIED while power on process is running."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.10" Date="2017-09-28" Author="HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: VMax, AMax and JMax can now be set on the servers and will be called in the _Firstscan by SetBasicParameter&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: Login for callback at CalcModel; So if kinematic changes new sw-limits can be set"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.9" Date="2017-01-27" Author="HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Improvement: before coupling, the result of the direct-kinematic will be checked, if it is in a defined window to the actual positions"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.8" Date="2016-10-14" Author="PalHar&#13;&#10;SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Coupling to a rotatory disc with MoveLinearBelt and MoveCurveBelt.&#13;&#10;2. Bugfix: In the function: MoveCurveRobotIntern all data defined by the pointer: pObstacle are stored locally to protect them from overwriting."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.7" Date="2016-04-06" Author="PalHar&#13;&#10;SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: New SetRobotParameter mode _NOT_CALC_BOTH_KINEMATICS_OPTIMIZE added.&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: All move commands have been expanded with a new input parameter MaxJerk for enabling different jerk values.&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: Method MoveLinearBelt uses the temporary profile buffer to insert its commands.&#13;&#10;4. Bugfix: code optimization for EDGE2 CPUs.&#13;&#10;5. Bugfix: The Spline in the function: MoveCurve starts at the Point defined by the parameter: HeightStart_relativ and ends at the Point defined by the parameter: HeightEnd_relativ.&#13;&#10;6. Improvement: Method ReadRobotParameter gets new parameter numbers _AXCOUNT_PROFILE, and _AXCOUNT_CALCMODEL.&#13;&#10;7. Improvement: MoveCircle works well with base coordinate systems now. It is possible to command 2D circles in base coordinates.&#13;&#10;8. Bugfix: the functions: MoveCurve, MoveCurveCoord, MoveCurveBelt, MoveCircle, and MoveCircleCoord are extended to deal with _VOID_POS as input-parameters.&#13;&#10;9. Bugfix: Restart of a NC file with the _LMCCNCInterpreter works after an axis error.&#13;&#10;10. Improvement: Ready for the new _LMCProfileBase enhancement: SetProfileParameter(ParNr:=_LMCPROF_ProfileInPos, Value:=1)"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.5" Date="2016-01-07" Author="SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: Method ReadRobotParameter gets new parameter numbers _AXCOUNT_PROFILE, and _AXCOUNT_CALCMODEL."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.4" Date="2016-01-07" Author="SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Bugfix: MoveLinearCoord and MoveCurveCoord never write and change the memory, which is given as input parameter pBeltData."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.3" Date="2015-12-10" Author="SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="Bugfix: If the belt coupling is active and if we program a MoveLinear to another coordinate system, then the belt coupling is lifted correctly."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.2" Date="2015-12-04" Author="SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: New mode _IS_CALCMODEL_CONNECTED for ReadRobotParameter().&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: New commands MoveCurve, MoveCurveCoord, and MoveCurveBelt.&#13;&#10;3. Bugfix: A linear robot without using _LMCCalcModelBase can be switched on, if its positions are outside of its software limits."/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.1" Date="2015-09-25" Author="RauAnd&#13;&#10;SatChr&#13;&#10;HasHan" Company="Sigmatek" Description="1. Improvement: The override of the axes is set correctly, also if some axes are locked to the _LMCProfile&#13;&#10;2. Improvement: DelayPowerOn() can no also deliver BUSY to do some userchecks&#13;&#10;3. Improvement: new methodes AxReadPosition(), AxSetAdjustment() and AxSetFollowMode()&#13;&#10;4. Improvement: new Bit PowerIsOn in RobotStatus&#13;&#10;5. Bugfix: Using the value _VOID_POS for destinations of move commands works also with base coordinate systems now&#13;&#10;6. Bugfix: Belt coupling with EDGE2 CPUs is threadsafe now&#13;&#10;7. Bugfix: Errors of kinematic axes can be receipted now&#13;&#10;8. Bugfix: While referencing the hardware axes, a RobotOff() command is executed faster now"/>
		<Dokumentation Revision="1.0" Date="2015-07-15" Author="FucHer&#13;&#10;HasHan&#13;&#10;PalHar&#13;&#10;SatChr" Company="Sigmatek" Description="creation"/>
